{
  "module": "Inference: prefill, decode and the cache",
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "kv-cache-size",
    "title": "How big the KV cache is",
    "summary": "The formula for the cache's size in bytes, each factor in it, and the worked example for Llama-2-7B: half a megabyte per token, about 2 GiB for a 4,096-token sequence.",
    "covers": ["kv-cache-size"],
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "lesson": "kv-cache",
        "reason": "This sizes the cache described there."
      },
      {
        "lesson": "multi-head",
        "reason": "The number of heads and their width set the size."
      }
    ]
  },
  "screens": [
    {
      "ref": "formula",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "How much memory does the cache take? For one sequence:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "latex": "\\text{bytes} = 2 \\cdot L \\cdot n \\cdot h_{kv} \\cdot d_{\\mathrm{head}} \\cdot b",
          "spoken": "bytes equals 2 times L times n times h k v times d head times b"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "where L is the number of layers, n the number of tokens, h_kv the number of K/V heads, d_head the width of each, and b the bytes per number."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 78)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "each-factor",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "text": "2",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": both K and V are stored."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "L",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": every layer has its own cache."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "n",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": one entry per token, so the cache grows with the text."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "h_kv · d_head",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": how much is stored for each token, in each layer, for each of K and V."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "text": "b",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "text": ": the bytes for each number, for example 2 for fp16."
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 78)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "llama-example",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Llama-2-7B has L = 32 layers, 32 K/V heads, d_head = 128 and stores fp16, which is 2 bytes per number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Per token: 2 × 32 × 32 × 128 × 2 = 524,288 bytes, which is 0.5 MiB."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 78)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "whole-sequence",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "For a whole sequence, multiply by n. With n = 4,096 tokens: 524,288 × 4,096 = 2,147,483,648 bytes, which is 2 GiB of cache."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "That is for a single sequence, on top of the memory the model's weights already take."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 78)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "linear-growth",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The formula is linear in n. "
            },
            {
              "text": "Double the text and you double the cache.",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " At 32,768 tokens the same model would need 16 GiB for one sequence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "This is why the cache, and not only the arithmetic, limits how long a text a model can handle. A later lesson returns to it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "Transformers in LLMs: mechanics and pipeline (flashkarte deck, cards 78)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
